        <body>
            <div xml:id="d192">

                <pb facs="0324" n="218" sameAs="frus:frus1906p1/pg218"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minister Rockhill to
                        the Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Peking</hi></placeName>, <hi rendition="#italic"><date
                                calendar="gregorian" when="1906-08-15">August 15,
                        1906</date>.</hi></dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 377.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In further reference to the subject of the
                    establishment at Antung of customs facilities, I have the honor to inclose
                    herewith copies of notes I have recently addressed to the Prince of Ch’ing.</p>
                <p>I have received replies to neither of these notes. Yesterday I called at the
                    Wai-wu Pu and asked that an early answer should, be sent me.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. W. Rockhill.</hi></signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d192-a1.xml" xpointer="d192-a1"/>
                <xi:include href="d192-a2.xml" xpointer="d192-a2"/>
